# Final Project Plan

## 1. Full-Stack Web Application
- Transformer and consumer monitoring dashboard
- Live simulated sensor readings
- Energy-loss percentage and threshold detection
- Alerts, graphs, reports, and history

## 2. Virtual Hardware Prototype
- Simulated ESP32 microcontroller
- Two current-measurement points (Transformer Input CT1 vs Consumer Aggregate CT2)
- Threshold-based anomaly detection on edge
- Simulated wireless alerts sent to backend (HTTP/REST / WebSocket)

## 3. Hardware Design Documents
- Circuit schematic (detailed pinouts, conditioning circuitry, sensors, ESP32)
- PCB layout (Gerber specifications, 2-layer PCB design, trace widths, silkscreen)
- 3D enclosure model (OpenSCAD parametric script + dimensional CAD drawings + cutouts for OLED & cable glands)
- Bill of materials (BOM) with part numbers, footprints, quantities, and cost estimates

## 4. Complete Project Documentation
- PRD, system architecture, database schema, API documentation, test cases, user guide, installation instructions, and final project report.
